  "id": "complete-case-analysis",
  "term": "complete-case analysis",
  "definition": "Complete-case analysis is an approach to missing outcome data that uses only participants with complete information and leaves out those with missing values. In the source, it is presented as a common comparison method that can give biased results when missingness is linked to unobserved factors affecting the outcome.",
